  I think the best way to handle a confirm option would be for someone 
to provide code to do it that could be included with the next patch level 
and selected via a switch in the makefile.  I don't think that such an 
option is necesary or desirable, but it is obvious that some people feel
it would be a valuable addition to the game.

  Actually, perhaps the best way to implement it would be to avoid the
issue altogether by providing a NO_POOLS option that would eliminate 
all pools except the moat.  I think that taking special care on the fortress
level is advisable anyways, and the having deadly pools only on the fortress
level would not represent a serious arbitrary death risk to most players.

(BTW, my pet peeve with pools, is exactly that: a pet peeve.  I hate it when
my dog or cat dies as a result of my quaffing at a fountain.  Since I can
go out of my wayy and avoid that happening, though, I wouldn't want the game
changed to reflect my playing habits (if I did, all players would start as
healers! ]-)                                                               )

